From: MinaKaramApex <Mina.Karam@apexmedical.ai>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:37:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] feat(openobserve): partial view updates default off

Upstream enables betaEnableViewUpdates by default unless a proxy is set (or
the bundle is the Salesforce build). The OpenObserve server has no handling
for the view_update event type, so the default is now false. An explicit
`betaEnableViewUpdates: true` is still honoured (the event bridge still
forces it off). Spec updated to match, serialized telemetry reports the
effective value.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../configuration/configuration.spec.ts       | 18 ++++++++++++-----
 .../src/domain/configuration/configuration.ts | 20 +++++++++----------
 2 files changed, 22 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)

diff --git a/packages/browser-rum-core/src/domain/configuration/configuration.spec.ts b/packages/browser-rum-core/src/domain/configuration/configuration.spec.ts
index cef61db99..d107fcb95 100644
--- a/packages/browser-rum-core/src/domain/configuration/configuration.spec.ts
+++ b/packages/browser-rum-core/src/domain/configuration/configuration.spec.ts
@@ -558,8 +558,9 @@ describe('validateAndBuildRumConfiguration', () => {
